IMPORT `P5-section-5`

-- P5-art-40-41-42: Chapter III Section 5, Articles 40 (harmonised standards and standardisation deliverables), 41 (common
-- specifications) and 42 (presumption of conformity with certain requirements). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026 (a plain-text rendering with no legal effect; src:N is its line N).
-- Group: General (Art 113 second paragraph, assumed: keel fork F-113-groups). Nothing here restates a date of Article 113 or 111.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text's own yes / no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (P5)"). Before the group applies, and where Art 111(2) saves the system, NOTHING.
-- Official-only duties (the Commission, a Member State) are encoded for what they decide; there is no seat for an official.

§ `Article 40: harmonised standards and standardisation deliverables`

§§ `Article 40(1): the presumption of conformity with harmonised standards`

-- Two limbs of one sentence: a high-risk AI system (the requirements of Section 2) and a general-purpose AI model (the obligations of
-- Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3). A presumption gives a legal effect; where its conditions are not met the text does not say the
-- system is not in conformity, so the answer is NOTHING (limited by its own wording: "to the extent that those standards cover").
-- src:640 | 1. High-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models which are in conformity with harmonised standards or parts thereof the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 shall be presumed to be in conformity with the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, with the obligations set out in of Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3, of this Regulation, to the extent that those standards cover those requirements or obligations.
@ref Art 40(1), high-risk AI system limb (src:640)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harmonised standard covers the requirement set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 40 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF       `Art 3(27) the standard is a harmonised standard` `the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`
                   AND `the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof`
                   AND `the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`
                   AND `the harmonised standard covers the requirement set out in Section 2`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be presumed ... to the extent that those standards cover those requirements"

-- src:640 | 1. High-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models which are in conformity with harmonised standards or parts thereof the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 shall be presumed to be in conformity with the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, with the obligations set out in of Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3, of this Regulation, to the extent that those standards cover those requirements or obligations.
@ref Art 40(1), general-purpose AI model limb (src:640)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the general-purpose AI model is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harmonised standard covers the obligation set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(1) the general-purpose AI model is presumed to be in conformity with the obligation set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF       `Art 3(27) the standard is a harmonised standard` `the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`
              AND `the general-purpose AI model is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof`
              AND `the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`
              AND `the harmonised standard covers the obligation set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be presumed ... to the extent that those standards cover those requirements or obligations"

§§ `Article 40(2) and (3): what the Commission and the participants in standardisation must do (no seat: officials; what they mean to a provider is Article 40(1))`

-- The party and the act of every rule of Articles 40 and 41 that names the Commission, a Member State or the participants.
-- None of these rules states a time limit or a consequence ("without undue delay" is no number of days), so no trace can reach BREACH:
-- they are listed in NOTES.md under "Rules with no breach path (P5)".
DECLARE `Art 40 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 40 the Commission`
    `Art 40 a participant in the standardisation process`

DECLARE `Art 40 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 40(2) issue standardisation requests`
    `Art 40(2) ask for deliverables on reporting and documentation processes`
    `Art 40(2) consult the Board and relevant stakeholders`
    `Art 40(2) specify that standards have to be clear and consistent`
    `Art 40(2) request evidence of best efforts`
    `Art 40(2) request standardisation deliverables`
    `Art 40(3) seek to promote investment and innovation in AI`

-- First subparagraph, first sentence. "as applicable" hands the Chapter V limb to the Commission's judgment: a plain input.
-- src:641 | 2. In accordance with Article 10 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, the Commission shall issue, without undue delay, standardisation requests covering all requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter and, as applicable, standardisation requests covering obligations set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3, of this Regulation.
@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, first sentence, limb (a) (src:641)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(2) the Commission must issue standardisation requests covering all requirements set out in Section 2` MEANS
    IF `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come

-- src:641 | 2. In accordance with Article 10 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, the Commission shall issue, without undue delay, standardisation requests covering all requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter and, as applicable, standardisation requests covering obligations set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3, of this Regulation.
@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, first sentence, limb (b) (src:641)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `standardisation requests covering obligations set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3 are applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(2) the Commission must issue standardisation requests covering obligations set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `standardisation requests covering obligations set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3 are applicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as applicable" (a condition the text introduces; the Commission's judgment is the input)

-- First subparagraph, second sentence: what the request must contain.
-- src:641 | The standardisation request shall also ask for deliverables on reporting and documentation processes to improve AI systems’ resource performance, such as reducing the high-risk AI system’s consumption of energy and of other resources during its lifecycle, and on the energy-efficient development of general-purpose AI models.
@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, second sentence (src:641)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(2) the standardisation request must also ask for deliverables on reporting and documentation processes` MEANS
    IF `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come

-- First subparagraph, third sentence: "When preparing a standardisation request": "when" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)).
-- src:641 | When preparing a standardisation request, the Commission shall consult the Board and relevant stakeholders, including the advisory forum.
@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, third sentence (src:641)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is preparing a standardisation request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(2) the Commission must consult the Board and relevant stakeholders` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the Commission is preparing a standardisation request`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When preparing a standardisation request"

-- Second subparagraph.
-- src:642 | When issuing a standardisation request to European standardisation organisations, the Commission shall specify that standards have to be clear, consistent, including with the standards developed in the various sectors for products covered by the existing Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, and aiming to ensure that high-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models placed on the market or put into service in the Union meet the relevant requirements or obligations laid down in this Regulation.
@ref Art 40(2) second subparagraph (src:642)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is issuing a standardisation request to European standardisation organisations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(2) the Commission must specify that standards have to be clear and consistent` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the Commission is issuing a standardisation request to European standardisation organisations`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When issuing a standardisation request to European standardisation organisations"

-- Third subparagraph.
-- src:643 | The Commission shall request the European standardisation organisations to provide evidence of their best efforts to fulfil the objectives referred to in the first and the second subparagraph of this paragraph in accordance with Article 24 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012.
@ref Art 40(2) third subparagraph (src:643)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 40(2) the Commission must request the European standardisation organisations to provide evidence of their best efforts` MEANS
    IF `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come

-- Fourth subparagraph, INSERTED by the Omnibus (▼M1): there is no as-enacted text. Version: as amended only.
-- src:645 | The Commission shall request, in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 of the European Parliament and of the Council (
-- src:646 | [^1]
-- src:647 | ) and without undue delay, the European standardisation organisations to develop standardisation deliverables, including, as appropriate, harmonised standards, to facilitate the joint compliance and presumption of conformity with the requirements or obligations set out in Chapter III, Sections 2 and 3 of this Regulation, and the relevant requirements and obligations laid down in the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I to this Regulation.
@ref Art 40(2) fourth subparagraph, inserted by the Omnibus (src:645-647)
