§§ `Article 40: the regulative rules (each names a party and an act; none states a time limit or a consequence)`

-- Where the provisions do not apply on the date asked nothing is owed (FULFILLED); otherwise the party must do the act.
@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, first sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(2) the Commission's duty to issue standardisation requests` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 40 the Commission` MUST `Art 40(2) issue standardisation requests`

@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, second sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(2) the Commission's duty to ask for deliverables on reporting and documentation processes` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 40 the Commission` MUST `Art 40(2) ask for deliverables on reporting and documentation processes`

@ref Art 40(2) first subparagraph, third sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(2) the Commission's duty to consult the Board and relevant stakeholders` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 40 the Commission` MUST `Art 40(2) consult the Board and relevant stakeholders`

@ref Art 40(2) second subparagraph
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(2) the Commission's duty to specify that standards have to be clear and consistent` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 40 the Commission` MUST `Art 40(2) specify that standards have to be clear and consistent`

@ref Art 40(2) third subparagraph
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(2) the Commission's duty to request evidence of best efforts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 40 the Commission` MUST `Art 40(2) request evidence of best efforts`

@ref Art 40(2) fourth subparagraph (as amended)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(2) the Commission's duty to request standardisation deliverables` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN FULFILLED  -- VERSION as enacted: the fourth subparagraph is not in the text, nothing is owed
         WHEN `as amended` THEN           -- VERSION as amended
             PARTY `Art 40 the Commission` MUST `Art 40(2) request standardisation deliverables`

@ref Art 40(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 40 party` `Art 40 act`
`Art 40(3) the duty of the participants in the standardisation process` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 40 a participant in the standardisation process` MUST `Art 40(3) seek to promote investment and innovation in AI`

§ `Article 41: common specifications`

§§ `Article 41(1): when the Commission may adopt implementing acts establishing common specifications`

-- A power ("may adopt") gated by "where the following conditions have been fulfilled": a "where" condition that fails answers JUST FALSE
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); NOTES.md split site (ii), fork F-41-1: the other reading is NOTHING, a grant limited by its own wording).
-- (a) is the request AND one of (i) to (iv); (b) is "and": no reference published and none expected within a reasonable period.
-- src:652 | 1. The Commission may adopt, implementing acts establishing common specifications for the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, for the obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V where the following conditions have been fulfilled:
-- src:653 | (a) the Commission has requested, pursuant to Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, one or more European standardisation organisations to draft a harmonised standard for the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter, or, as applicable, for the obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V, and:
-- src:654 | (i) the request has not been accepted by any of the European standardisation organisations; or
-- src:655 | (ii) the harmonised standards addressing that request are not delivered within the deadline set in accordance with Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012; or
-- src:656 | (iii) the relevant harmonised standards insufficiently address fundamental rights concerns; or
-- src:657 | (iv) the harmonised standards do not comply with the request; and
-- src:658 | (b) no reference to harmonised standards covering the requirements referred to in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, the obligations referred to in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V has been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, and no such reference is expected to be published within a reasonable period.
@ref Art 41(1), first subparagraph, points (a) and (b) (src:652-658)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has requested, pursuant to Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, one or more European standardisation organisations to draft a harmonised standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request has not been accepted by any of the European standardisation organisations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harmonised standards addressing that request are not delivered within the deadline set in accordance with Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant harmonised standards insufficiently address fundamental rights concerns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harmonised standards do not comply with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no reference to harmonised standards covering those requirements or obligations has been published in the Official Journal of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no such reference is expected to be published within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 41(1) the Commission may adopt implementing acts establishing common specifications` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF       `the Commission has requested, pursuant to Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, one or more European standardisation organisations to draft a harmonised standard`
              AND (    `the request has not been accepted by any of the European standardisation organisations`
                    OR `the harmonised standards addressing that request are not delivered within the deadline set in accordance with Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`
                    OR `the relevant harmonised standards insufficiently address fundamental rights concerns`
                    OR `the harmonised standards do not comply with the request`)
              AND `no reference to harmonised standards covering those requirements or obligations has been published in the Official Journal of the European Union`
              AND `no such reference is expected to be published within a reasonable period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the following conditions have been fulfilled" (reading (b), fork F-41-1)

-- Second paragraph of paragraph 1.
-- src:659 | When drafting the common specifications, the Commission shall consult the advisory forum referred to in Article 67.
@ref Art 41(1), second subparagraph (src:659)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is drafting the common specifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 41(1) the Commission must consult the advisory forum` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the Commission is drafting the common specifications`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When drafting the common specifications"

-- Paragraph 2: the Commission informs the committee of Article 22 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 before preparing a draft implementing act.
-- src:661 | 2. Before preparing a draft implementing act, the Commission shall inform the committee referred to in Article 22 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 that it considers the conditions laid down in paragraph 1 of this Article to be fulfilled.
@ref Art 41(2) (src:661)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission is preparing a draft implementing act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 41(2) the Commission must inform the committee that it considers the conditions to be fulfilled` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the Commission is preparing a draft implementing act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before preparing a draft implementing act"

§§ `Article 41(3): the presumption of conformity with common specifications`

-- "referred to in paragraph 1": common specifications established by an implementing act under paragraph 1 (a plain input).
-- src:662 | 3. High-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models which are in conformity with the common specifications referred to in paragraph 1, or parts of those specifications, shall be presumed to be in conformity with the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, to comply with the obligations referred to in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V, to the extent those common specifications cover those requirements or those obligations.
@ref Art 41(3), high-risk AI system limb (src:662)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the set of technical specifications is a common specification established by an implementing act under Article 41(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the common specifications or parts of those specifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the common specifications cover the requirement set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 41(3) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 41 3)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF       `the set of technical specifications is a common specification established by an implementing act under Article 41(1)`
                   AND `the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the common specifications or parts of those specifications`
                   AND `the common specifications cover the requirement set out in Section 2`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be presumed ... to the extent those common specifications cover those requirements"

-- src:662 | 3. High-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models which are in conformity with the common specifications referred to in paragraph 1, or parts of those specifications, shall be presumed to be in conformity with the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, to comply with the obligations referred to in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V, to the extent those common specifications cover those requirements or those obligations.
