    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the provider does not comply with the common specifications referred to in Article 41(1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where providers ... do not comply with the common specifications"

-- Has the duty been met? The justification must show technical solutions that meet the requirements or obligations "to a level at least equivalent".
-- A bare "shall duly justify" not done: JUST FALSE, case by case (fork F-41-5). "duly" is a judgment: a plain input.
-- src:664 | 5. Where providers of high-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models do not comply with the common specifications referred to in paragraph 1, they shall duly justify that they have adopted technical solutions that meet the requirements referred to in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, comply with the obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V to a level at least equivalent thereto.
@ref Art 41(5), the duty met (src:664)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provider does not comply with the common specifications referred to in Article 41(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has duly justified that it has adopted technical solutions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those technical solutions meet the requirements or comply with the obligations to a level at least equivalent to the common specifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 41(5) the provider has met the duty to duly justify the technical solutions` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF NOT `the provider does not comply with the common specifications referred to in Article 41(1)`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only where the provider does not comply; here it complies
         ELSE IF       `the provider has duly justified that it has adopted technical solutions`
                   AND `those technical solutions meet the requirements or comply with the obligations to a level at least equivalent to the common specifications`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they shall duly justify that they have adopted technical solutions that meet the requirements ... to a level at least equivalent thereto" (a bare "shall" not done, case by case)

