§§ `Article 41: the regulative rules (each names a party and an act; none states a time limit or a consequence)`

DECLARE `Art 41 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 41 the Commission`
    `Art 41 a Member State`

DECLARE `Art 41 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 41(1) consult the advisory forum`
    `Art 41(1) adopt implementing acts establishing common specifications`
    `Art 41(2) inform the committee`
    `Art 41(4) assess the harmonised standard`
    `Art 41(4) repeal the implementing act or the part of it`
    `Art 41(6) inform the Commission`
    `Art 41(6) amend the implementing act`

-- A permission: "may adopt". A MAY has no breach to reach (the brief's list "Rules with no breach path").
@ref Art 41(1) first subparagraph
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(1) the Commission's permission to adopt implementing acts establishing common specifications` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 the Commission` MAY `Art 41(1) adopt implementing acts establishing common specifications`

@ref Art 41(1) second subparagraph
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(1) the Commission's duty to consult the advisory forum` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 the Commission` MUST `Art 41(1) consult the advisory forum`

@ref Art 41(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(2) the Commission's duty to inform the committee` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 the Commission` MUST `Art 41(2) inform the committee`

@ref Art 41(4) first sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(4) the Commission's duty to assess the harmonised standard` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 the Commission` MUST `Art 41(4) assess the harmonised standard`

@ref Art 41(4) second sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(4) the Commission's duty to repeal the implementing act` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 the Commission` MUST `Art 41(4) repeal the implementing act or the part of it`

@ref Art 41(6) first sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(6) the Member State's duty to inform the Commission` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 a Member State` MUST `Art 41(6) inform the Commission`

@ref Art 41(6) second sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 41 party` `Art 41 act`
`Art 41(6) the Commission's duty to amend the implementing act` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked
    ELSE PARTY `Art 41 the Commission` MUST `Art 41(6) amend the implementing act`

-- The provider's duty of Art 41(5): the party is a core Role, the act is the provider's own.
DECLARE `Art 41(5) provider act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 41(5) duly justify the technical solutions adopted`

@ref Art 41(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider does not comply with the common specifications referred to in Article 41(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 41(5) provider act`
`Art 41(5) the provider's duty to duly justify the technical solutions adopted` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 41 5)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): nothing is owed, because Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the provisions do not apply on the date asked, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF `the provider does not comply with the common specifications referred to in Article 41(1)`
              THEN PARTY Provider MUST `Art 41(5) duly justify the technical solutions adopted`
              ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: "Where providers ... do not comply" is not met

